# This repo is edited from a Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true) but every shell
# script here runs under Linux -- inside the ESP-IDF Docker container (build.sh,
# setup_espidf.sh) or under WSL2 (flash.sh, monitor.sh, setup-ch340.sh). CRLF
# silently breaks those: `#!/bin/bash\r` breaks the shebang lookup and every
# line's trailing \r merges into the next token. The identical failure was
# WITNESSED on the sibling ../aloop project, where an edited kernel/rt-tune.sh
# picked up CRLF and silently stopped working on the real device with no error
# anywhere in the pipeline (CI stayed green; only the hardware misbehaved).
# Force LF for every text format actually consumed by a POSIX interpreter,
# regardless of what any individual clone's core.autocrlf is set to.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
sdkconfig text eol=lf
sdkconfig.defaults text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers genuinely want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binaries must never be touched by line-ending normalization at all.
*.bin binary
*.elf binary
*.so binary
*.a binary
*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.mid binary
